/* First run */
"onboarding.window.title" = "First run";
"onboarding.step1.title" = "Lazy Switcher";
"onboarding.step1.body" = "Spots text typed in the wrong keyboard layout and fixes it.\n\nghbdtn  →  привет\nруддщ   →  hello\n\nIt switches the layout too, so the rest of the sentence comes out right.\n\nFree. Runs on your machine. Nothing you type is written to disk or sent anywhere.";
"onboarding.step1.primary" = "Next";
"onboarding.step2.title" = "Permission needed";
"onboarding.step2.body" = "macOS will not let a program see what you type without your consent. That is as it should be, and here is what the consent means in practice.\n\nThe app sees keystrokes. That is why it is built so that what you type lives in memory for a few seconds and is then wiped — it goes into no file, no log and no crash report.\n\nWhat it does not see: when the system turns on secure input — at the login window, in a password manager, in an ordinary app's password field — the keystrokes simply never reach it. Not “we choose not to look”, but physically absent.\n\nAnd, honestly, the limit of that: on websites, no browser turns that mode on. There a password field is recognised from the page's accessibility markup — which works in Safari, and does not work in Chrome or Firefox, so in those only manual correction is available by default.\n\nPress the button, switch “Lazy Switcher” on in the list, and come back here.";
"onboarding.step2.primary" = "Open Accessibility settings";
"onboarding.step2.secondary" = "Skip";
"onboarding.step3.title" = "All set";
"onboarding.step3.body" = "Everything works.\n\nType a word in the wrong layout and press space — it fixes itself, as long as the word is longer than four characters.\n\nYour chosen gesture (double Shift by default):\n• text is selected — the whole selection is converted;\n• a correction just happened — it is undone, and the word is remembered as “never change”;\n• otherwise — the last word is corrected.\n\nLeft and right Shift together pauses the app.\n\nAll of this is adjustable in Settings: the gesture, the sound and the list of apps.";
"onboarding.step3.primary" = "Get started";
"onboarding.step3.secondary" = "Open Settings";
"menu.status.paused" = "Paused — press left and right Shift together";
